 ## Overview
-Depth Rendering with Weighted Average computes a depth map for 3D Gaussian Splatting by calculating a weighted average of Gaussian depths along a ray, where the weights are determined by the alpha-compositing process [S1, S2]. It differs from [Depth Rendering with Constant Opacity](7462-depth-rendering-with-constant-opacity.md) by allowing opacity to influence the depth accumulation, which can lead to depth ambiguity at sharp edges or with misplaced "floaters" [S1, S2]. It is distinct from [Normalized Depth Rendering](8298-normalized-depth-rendering.md) and [Depth Rendering with Variable Opacity](12622-depth-rendering-with-variable-opacity.md) in its reliance on standard alpha-blending mechanics rather than normalization or variable opacity constraints [S1, S2].
+Depth Rendering with Weighted Average computes a depth map for 3D Gaussian Splatting by calculating a weighted average of Gaussian depths along a ray, where the weights are determined by the alpha-compositing process [S1, S2]. It differs from [Depth Rendering with Constant Opacity](7462-depth-rendering-with-constant-opacity.md) by allowing opacity to influence the depth accumulation, which can lead to depth ambiguity at sharp edges or with misplaced "floaters" [S2]. It is distinct from [Normalized Depth Rendering](8298-normalized-depth-rendering.md) and [Depth Rendering with Variable Opacity](12622-depth-rendering-with-variable-opacity.md) in its reliance on standard alpha-blending mechanics rather than normalization or variable opacity constraints [S1, S2].
 
